WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.440
What turns an undead into a hollow?

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.120
Is it a passing centuries in a neverending life?

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.280
The experience of dying hundreds of times?

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.940
Or is it those things coupled with a loss of hope?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.460
Firelink is often the last place the heroes visit before they hollow.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.480
It's the gateway to many dangerous places.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:25.080
Most undead in Lordran have a purpose that they strive towards, before hollowing.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.400
However, there is one who is content to wait until his sanity slips away.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.120
The apathy of this man is kept within Firelink Shrine,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.900
where he simply watches.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.600
Heroes come and go, some never return

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.940
and he remains.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.820
At least nothing will bother him once he goes hollow.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.780
"Oh, did you see him?

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.240
Big Hat Logan,

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.160
the legendary sorcerer,

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.260
in the flesh!

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.160
This place is simply mad!

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.680
Legendary heroes popping up left and right...

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:59.900
They're making me feel quite inadequate, to be honest."

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:05.400
"Oh, have you seen that terribly morose lass?

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:06.980
The Fire Keeper.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:11.480
She's stuck keeping that bonfire lit. Sad, really.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:15.540
She's mute and bound to this forsaken place."

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.320
"How did that silly sorcerer's apprentice end up?

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.520
You know, the one always prattling on about Master Logan.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.160
He left for the Undead Burg, but never came back.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.380
Servers him right.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.960
If even Old Big Hat can't make it out there...

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.920
...what chance does he have?

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.100
I hope he enjoys his new life as a hollow."

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.800
"How did that raggedy old chum end up?

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:46.820
You know, the one who idolized some godmother of pyromancy.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.820
He left for Blighttown,

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:50.800
but never came back."

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.780
"Did you hear about the maiden?

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:59.780
The virtuous lass came back alone, and in absolute tatters…

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.480
Did her followers die, or was she abandoned?

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:04.960
Who knows...

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:09.100
But I suppose we've heard the last from "M'lady"."

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.420
"Did you ring the second bell?"

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.700
"That is incredible, I must say…

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.200
But now we have a new problem.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:23.420
It's noisy, it snores, and its breath is lethal…

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.040
And I was really beginning to like it here.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.880
Sigh… Maybe it's time I do something about it…"

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:39.200
"Well,

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.400
what are you going to do?

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.480
I've already decided.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.360
I don't really care.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:47.820
I am simply...

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:49.720
...crestfallen."

